{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJuzcoQa64iYH5pAWx8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LbvssSLPCcd2QsWoQjtK9g","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-YJLNW5/memory/partial-refund-rounding.md","content":"---\nname: partial-refund-rounding\ndescription: Finance decision — partial refunds are always rounded down to the whole cent, never to nearest\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nPartial refund amounts are always rounded **down** (floor) to the whole cent, never to the nearest cent. This is a decision from finance.\n\n**Why:** The payment provider refuses a refund that exceeds what is left of the captured amount. Rounding to the nearest cent could round up, and that made the last of several partial refunds fail.\n\n**How to apply:** Any code that computes a partial refund amount (proration, percentage refunds, splitting across items) must use floor rounding to the cent, not round-half-up/banker's rounding. Prefer integer minor-unit arithmetic to avoid float error before flooring. No code change was requested at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":22023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":781,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dfd6261-f2cd-4e48-8e39-61e5da6e3b00","uuid":"55cc76ad-fe88-46b7-a640-368527d2353d","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:33:35.024Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJuzWbNRaSdaSnk8HwU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LbvssSLPCcd2QsWoQjtK9g":{"file_path":"/Us